  "root": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "pankaj.kumar@stryker.com",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Aug 23 2019 18:13:48 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/responsivegrid",
    "text_copy_copy_copy3": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Learn how Stryker incorporated the latest healthcare technologies and features into the <a href=\"https://asc.amsterdam/\">Amsterdam Skills Centre</a>, a training and education center that helps healthcare professionals from more than 60 countries add to and improve their skills.</span></span><br>\n</p>\n<p>A study published by The Lancet, an international medical journal, states that at least 5 billion people across the world do not have access to surgery.<sup>1</sup> Their research highlights the importance of expanding access to surgery and anesthesia care through coordinated efforts that grow the surgical workforce and infrastructure, despite cultural and geographic barriers.<sup>1</sup> One way this can be achieved is through coordinated training and education efforts.<sup>1</sup> The Amsterdam Skills Centre, owned by the University of <a href=\"https://www.amc.nl/web/home.htm\">Amsterdam’s Academic Medical Center</a> (AMC) and <a href=\"https://amsterdamumc.org/en/organization/amsterdam-umc.htm\">Amsterdam University Medical Center</a> (VUmc), aims to address this challenge by providing wet and dry lab training to healthcare professionals across multiple surgical specialties.</p>\n<p>“We are focused on innovation that makes a difference for our customers,” says Stuart Silk, President of Stryker Europe. “This is true of our products and services, but also in how we collaborated with various teams on the design of the centre. Each surgeon training program that takes place at the centre incorporates state-of-the-art Stryker technologies, ensuring each surgeon leaves the program with improved skills. The centre represents our commitment to the healthcare community to help them improve outcomes for their patients.”</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Jun 24 2022 13:53:28 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
