    "text_167550914232333_638755144": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:title": "Tour",
      "cq:masterBuildingBlock": true,
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Jun 24 2022 14:00:42 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "cq/experience-fragments/editor/components/buildingblock",
      "text_167550914232333_638755144749315702189894": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
        "text": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\"><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\">2.</span> Wet and dry labs provide life-like training</span></span></p>\n<p>The opportunity for healthcare professionals to train outside of hospitals means more efficient use of hospital’s resources and capacity, which allows healthcare facilities to focus on what matters most, the treatment of more patients. The centre has two wet and dry labs that can accommodate 6 surgical stations each, with the option to combine the two labs for larger training events. Each lab is fully equipped with Stryker’s latest healthcare solutions and Fix for Life, a cadaveric innovation that provides surgeons with a life-like cadaveric experience.<sup>2</sup> It helps prepare residents and surgeons for real-life practice while also reducing trainees’ exposure to pathogens.<sup>2</sup></p>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Jun 29 2022 19:36:13 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
